<p>Havana Club, a basement nightclub for years, built its success on its wonderful reputation for food, service, ambiance. Like the Hotel McKenzie/Patterson Hotel in Bismarck, it was a place where many a political, business (legal and otherwise!) deals took place. Leo Guon left the business to his son when he died in November 1961, but he was not as enthusiastic about the food and service industry as his father. Lacking much oversite, the business' reputation deteriorated. Finances became tight, FICA taxes were not paid and the IRS closed the club in July of 1964.</p>

