<p>Barry and Esther Davis bought the Havana Club and reopened it on September 14, 1964. They had been approached by interested parties, including creditors, who wished the establishment to remain open and assisted with the deal's financing. Barry Davis had provided muscial entertainment at the site for years, and Esther had worked as a food hostess at another local nightclub.</p>

